  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Clinique Vétérinaire de La Clauvade, in Cuers, is a large practice with 15 vets and 19 veterinary assistants — unlike UVDelta 83 or V2U Toulon, this is not a pure emergency clinic: it's a regular practice (preventive medicine, imaging, general and orthopaedic surgery, oncology, senior check-ups, gentle hospitalisation, on-site lab tests) that, according to its own statements, also runs a 24/7 on-call rota on top of its usual consultations. This emergency status is stated on a dedicated page of the official website (vetocuers.com/urgences/) and is consistent with matching client reviews ("operated on in the middle of the night", professional welcome even on a Sunday, 4.8/5 rating) — but it remains a self-declared claim by the practice, not an independent confirmation in the strict sense, even though no negative signal of the "unreachable at night" kind was found.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Outside regular hours (Monday-Saturday 7:30am-7:30pm), calling the usual number puts you through to that day's on-call team. This is a good option if you're already a patient of this clinic or if you're in the Cuers / Pierrefeu-du-Var area. The only minor point flagged in reviews: the phone reception is sometimes described as overloaded during the day — this concerns the daytime front desk, not the night on-call service.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: for a genuine night-time emergency far from Cuers, UVDelta 83 (Puget-sur-Argens) or V2U (Toulon) — dedicated emergency practices — may be quicker to reach depending on where you are in the Var.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Cuers and Pierrefeu-du-Var are accessible from route de Nice.</p>
